title: International Relations
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: international_relations_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; international_relations_timer += 12;
card-image: img/international.jpg
max-visits: 4
#subtitle: Connecting with our fellow center-left parties all over the globe.

At the Progressive Alliance, we can contact and connect with fellow progressive and center-left parties globally.

- @liberals: Learn legislative compromise from the Canadian Liberals
- @nordic: Integrate aspects of the Nordic Model into our platform.
- @spd: Learn coalition-building from the German SPD.
- @pt: Refine our welfare messaging and policies with help from the Brazilian Workers' Party.
- @israel: Make connections with the 'zionist-left' in Israel.
- @return: There are more pressing issues at home...
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; conservative_dissent -= 5

We have close ties with the Liberals, but still much to learn from their skill at governing even with a minroity.

@nordic
subtitle: -1 resources 
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: socialist_strength += 5; populism += 3; socialist_dissent -= 5; progressive_dissent -= 5; conservative_dissent += 5; resources -= 1

The Nordic social democrats have done a stellar job at marketing welfare, and we have also found it to be easier to pitch a "Nordic Model" than social democracy. 

@spd
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: socialist_dissent -= 5; progressive_dissent -= 5; mainstream_dissent -= 5; conservative dissent -= 5; populism -= 5

The German Social Democrats have demonstrated effectiveness at holding together a broad coalition electorally, as well as building broad coalitions in the Bundestag. We can learn much from them, especially regarding our own internal factionalism.

@pt
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; populism += 4; socialist_dissent -= 5; progressive_dissent -= 2; conservative_dissent += 5

The Workers' Party in Brazil is a shining example of the success of economic populism. They could help us refine and expand our own economic messaging and policymaking.

@israel
subtitle: -1 resources [? if year is 2018 : - The israeli Legislative Elections are upcoming... could our support make a difference? ?][? if year = 2019 and month < 4 : The Israeli Legislative Elections are upcoming... could our support make a difference? ?]
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1

The Israeli Labor Party and Meretz Party align with us somewhat, but there is still ground to be made. Perhaps enough cooperation could even reflect positively in Israeli politics...

@return

Who cares about the rest of the world? All that matters is U S A!!
